# Who reviews what the agents and the pipeline depend on. Prompts, conventions and the config are code: a change to
# them changes what every future run does, so it needs an owner's review like any other change.
# Replace @your-org/qa-owners with a real team (Settings > Teams) or a list of logins.

# The pipeline's configuration and the documents the agents read.
/qa.config.json                 @your-org/qa-owners
/docs/test-conventions.md       @your-org/qa-owners
/docs/product-brief.md          @your-org/qa-owners

# The workflows that call the engine, and what they may touch.
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/qa-owners
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @your-org/qa-owners

# The shared layers of the suite. Specs under tests/ are reviewed by whoever owns the feature.
/fixtures/                      @your-org/qa-owners
/pages/                         @your-org/qa-owners
/playwright.config.ts           @your-org/qa-owners
